proof.text:
For the realized counit, the definition of $d$ gives $d_{j^*H}^{-1}=\mathcal L_X(r_{j^*H})\circ u_{j_!j^*H}$. Substitute this into the proposed equation and combine the three consecutive $\mathcal L_X$-images. By Step 4 the left side is
$$u_H^{-1}\circ\mathcal L_X\bigl(\epsilon^S_{\mathcal R_XH}\circ J_j(s_H)\circ r_{j^*H}\bigr)\circ u_{j_!j^*H}
=u_H^{-1}\circ\mathcal L_X\mathcal R_X(\epsilon^o_H)\circ u_{j_!j^*H}
=\epsilon^o_H.$$
The last equality is naturality of the same actual unit [lem-coef-derived-system-evaluation-calculus]. Completeness of $H,j^*H,j_!j^*H$ follows from the hypotheses and Step 2. The unit and counit equations therefore identify the realized adjunction with $j_!\dashv j^*$ through $d,b$. Every reduction comparison and equation was constructed in the strict system category and then localized; no arbitrary reconstruction isomorphism or equality-detection by evaluation was used.
